// RECEIPTS, NOT UPSTREAM FACT (DESIGN section 3). What the two H11SSL units' BMCs answered to read-only
// requests, keyed by BMC MAC like gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit_observation, and the readings
// gunbc.bmc.supermicro_bmc_read folds out of them. Nothing here was written to a BMC.
//
// UNIT 1 (BMC 192.168.1.252, MAC ac:1f:6b:e3:f5:7b), 2026-10-27, taken by merry-fox-82 with an
// operator-supplied credential that is in no file. Redfish: curl GETs from the session host; IPMI:
// ipmitool -I lanplus -C 3 from h11-a16 (192.168.1.202). Each capture's body is committed verbatim as
// relayed; the HTTP status of each Redfish GET is the relay's status line, carried on its row below. The
// manifest is the authority for which file answered which request; each read checks the file's sha256.
//
// TWO READINGS ON THIS CAPTURE THAT ARE THE FIRMWARE'S, NOT THE HOST'S: every Memory member reports
// RankCount equal to its member index (1..8) and MaxTDPMilliWatts values from 0 to 20480000 on identical
// RDIMMs. Neither is decoded by the Memory reader, and neither is read as a fact about the modules.
//
// UNIT 2 (BMC 192.168.1.254, MAC ac:1f:6b:e3:f6:22): the first-contact CGI pages already committed
// (artifacts/bmc/h11ssl-unit2-first-contact-*), and its Redfish root, refused unlicensed. Its HTTP status
// was not recorded. Unit 2 was unreachable on 2026-10-27, so it has no IPMI reading.
type SupermicroCapture { path: NonEmptyStr, sha256: NonEmptyStr, request: NonEmptyStr, http_status: Int? }

